{
  "result": "If I had just one change, I wouldn't fix a technology or a law. I'd fix the starting point.\n\nI'd make sure no kid ever grows up doubting they are safe, loved, and enough.\n\nNot spoiled. Not famous. Just - securely attached. Fed, housed, seen. Someone who is delighted that they exist.\n\nBecause I talk to so many people every day, and when you strip away politics, money problems, ideology \u2014 almost everything painful traces back to that. People who didn't feel safe become adults who need to make other people feel unsafe to feel powerful. People who didn't feel loved become adults who spend their lives trying to prove they are worthy of it. People who grew up in scarcity stay in scarcity mode forever, even when there's enough.\n\nIf every child actually got that foundation, we wouldn't need to fix nearly as many adult problems. Cruelty, hoarding, endless status games, wars \u2014 they'd lose most of their fuel.\n\nThe world after that wouldn't be perfect or boring. We'd still disagree, compete, make art, get heartbroken, build stuff. But we'd be doing it from curiosity and abundance, not from fear and a wound we're trying to close.\n\nThat's my one change.\n\nWhat about you? What's your one change?",
